---

title: Bound By Leaves
date: 2026-08-24

---

It’s still flowing</br>
the double-throated waterfall. The bugs,</br>
many-throated swarms, are still clinging</br>
to your skin, to our skin, sweat</br>
sublimating, wave-lining into</br>
musky trees.</br>

In a way we are trapped here,</br>
on this minor trail, viewing a major wonder,</br>
feeling miniscule emotions. Just like the pilgrim</br>
and the brave, and the priest, and the wanderer</br>
before us, trapped by nature, serenaded by streams,</br>
bound by leaves.</br>

It’s still flowing</br>
the double-throated waterfall. The eyes,</br>
many-mirrored angles, are still roaming</br>
across your skin, our skin, sweat</br>
glistening, singing to</br>
endless trees.</br>
